ksnip-pyqt6-ocr for Debian

This package is an upstream/GitHub add-on for ksnip-pyqt6. It installs an
optional Model Manager that creates a private virtual environment and installs
PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR from PyPI at runtime, after an explicit user action.

It is not part of the Debian main archive. A package that downloads and
installs executable Python code at runtime does not meet the main-area
self-containment requirements, so the core ksnip-pyqt6 package must remain
usable without this plugin.

The plugin only configures the core Script OCR backend. It does not add a
build-time dependency on Paddle to the core package.
